<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mark Carney</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mark Carney is a Canadian economist and politician who was governor of the Bank of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> from 2008 to 2013 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-england">Bank of England</a> from 2013 to 2020. Elected leader of the Liberal Party, he became prime minister of Canada in March 2025 and won the federal election of April 2025, held amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> tariffs and talk of annexation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mark-carney.jpg" alt="Mark Carney" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bryan Berlin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mark_Carney_Argentina_v_Spain_19_July_2026-303_(3x4_close_up_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
